Subject: [PATCH 02298/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE B3 (ARC
 NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY 2026-06-17) -- E3 EXECUTABLE-WORLD-MODEL
 solves of tr87 AND ft09, +1 level (L1) EACH, looped with a checkpoint per
 game + a hard per-game wall-time cap (breadth-of-progress beats an
 all-or-nothing single-game swing). Same harness as exp4327/exp4328
 (arXiv:2605.05138; the codex agent induces + refines a Python world model per
 game, the Carnot WorldModelVerifier grounds it, plan_and_execute). Both are
 deep-tail games graph-explore NO-ADVANCEd (mechanic-limited); gpt-5.5 solved
 both in the SOTA paper. The codex agent IS the proposer (WRITES
 results/arc_e3/<game>/world_model.py per game; NO nested CodexProposer). HARD
 gate per game: offline_reproduced=true AND reproduced_levels>=1. An honest
 partial per game (best verifier_accuracy + the residual mismatch class as a
 missing-world-model-rule gap) is PROGRESS. Report a per-game scorecard.
 verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded ARC progress, NOT a moat). NO TRM
 training; NO leaderboard submission; checkpoint after EACH game so a
 window-exhaustion preserves the first game's result.

